From 32c923558609ddbe42164088fd4c337d4cca4d50 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 17:48:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat: add migration management system for multi-tenant sync
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- Add src/lib/db/migration-registry.ts: TypeScript registry of all
  idempotent DDL migrations (0001–0056) so they can be applied from
  code without manual SQL Editor access.

- Add src/app/api/super-admin/migrations/route.ts:
  GET  — lists all migrations with applied/pending status
  POST — applies all pending migrations in order, stops on first error
  Both endpoints are super_admin-only. The tracker table
  (hrms_schema_migrations) is auto-created on first call.

- Update src/app/api/super-admin/health/route.ts: include a migration
  status check so the health dashboard warns when pending migrations
  exist, directing the super admin to apply them.

Because all tenants (YC, YPC, and future clients) share a single
Supabase database, running migrations once from the super admin panel
keeps every tenant in sync automatically.

